00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.133
- If you don't
use them properly,

00:10:28.133 --> 00:10:29.467
you will lose.
- [Tim] Right.

00:10:29.467 --> 00:10:32.000
- If there's a nail that I have
to put in the ground but I take

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.066
the wrench and I hit it when
the hammer was right there,

00:10:35.066 --> 00:10:36.800
it still comes down
to the practitioner.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:37.567
- Mhmmm.

00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:39.266
- And you have to
be good at your craft

00:10:39.266 --> 00:10:40.500
and you have to love...

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.200
If you don't love sales,
if you don't love it,

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.600
you have no chance
'cause it's so hard.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:46.400
It's so painful.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.367
There's so much rejection.
- [Tim] Right.

00:10:49.367 --> 00:10:51.166
- So those are the
things I think about.

00:10:51.166 --> 00:10:53.600
So technology clear
enabler as you've just said.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.433
- [Gary] Yes.

00:10:54.433 --> 00:10:56.567
- The person is
equally important--

00:10:56.567 --> 00:10:57.667
- [Gary] More important.

00:10:57.667 --> 00:11:00.333
- Right and going back to--
- More important.

00:11:00.333 --> 00:11:02.033
I apologize for
jumping in but let me

00:11:02.033 --> 00:11:03.333
make it perfectly straight.

00:11:03.333 --> 00:11:06.700
If I go play Roger Federer right
now in tennis and I have the

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.767
greatest tennis
racket ever made.

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:12.500
Like taken from the
Mars' new like resources.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.133
- [Tim] Right.

00:11:13.133 --> 00:11:16.600
- And he took a John
McEnroe 1974 tennis racket,

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:19.400
he would whip my ass.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.367
I'm crushing salespeople
that have every Salesforce,

00:11:22.367 --> 00:11:25.000
every one of your
competitors, 37 features,

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.533
upgraded, went to
every pro conference,

00:11:27.533 --> 00:11:28.867
watching this.

00:11:28.867 --> 00:11:31.000
I will beat their ass in
sales every day of the week.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.100
- [Tim] Right.
- Pure talent.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.700
- Right. So Gary, look,
we're nearly up on time.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.800
Would love any closing
thoughts from you for

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.433
sales professionals,
whether at a startup,

00:11:38.433 --> 00:11:39.266
at an enterprise.

00:11:39.266 --> 00:11:41.834
What should they go
out and do today, tomorrow?

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:43.300
- I look at
sales very differently

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.266
than the far majority.

00:11:44.266 --> 00:11:47.600
I think way too many
salespeople are inpatient.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.667
I think way too many
salespeople are transactional.

00:11:50.667 --> 00:11:53.934
I think way too many salespeople
are lowest common denominator.

00:11:53.934 --> 00:11:58.433
Spam, blast LinkedIn,
email bulk,

00:11:58.433 --> 00:12:00.066
business card,
business card, business card.

00:12:00.066 --> 00:12:02.166
So I think I've got a
different tactic on sales.

00:12:02.166 --> 00:12:03.400
- Mhmmm.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.967
- But don't get it
twisted, it's what I am.

00:12:04.967 --> 00:12:07.633
If you're not
happy with your upside,

00:12:07.633 --> 00:12:10.433
if you are not fully fulfilled.

00:12:10.433 --> 00:12:12.834
I think a lot of what
you heard from me today,

00:12:12.834 --> 00:12:15.233
I'm doing things
were reverse of you.

00:12:15.233 --> 00:12:17.367
I think a lot of you are doing
things that are directly in

00:12:17.367 --> 00:12:18.233
front of you.

00:12:18.233 --> 00:12:19.834
Numbers that they
put in front of you,

00:12:19.834 --> 00:12:22.800
you're trying to achieve that
because you have a beach house

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.600
you want to buy or
go on that vacation.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:27.967
Sales is a funny game if
you work in a big company.

00:12:27.967 --> 00:12:31.834
They manipulate
numbers to create your actions.

00:12:31.834 --> 00:12:35.967
I believe that the best
salespeople are doing things in

00:12:35.967 --> 00:12:37.266
a different way.

00:12:37.266 --> 00:12:40.834
I think you need to care
about the customer for real,

00:12:40.834 --> 00:12:44.867
reverse engineer them and give
them what they need and so

00:12:44.867 --> 00:12:48.166
I have a funny
feeling that for 87.9%,

00:12:48.166 --> 00:12:52.100
arbitrary number, that 87.9% of
the people watching right now,

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.667
I'm a better salesperson
than you because I'm the

00:12:53.667 --> 00:12:57.700
anti-salesperson and I think
that's the best salesperson.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:58.567
Think about that.

00:12:58.567 --> 00:13:00.900
Think about how you give
yourself air cover to not do

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:04.100
behavior that is short-term.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.333
Please understand that the world
has changed and the attention of

00:13:07.333 --> 00:13:08.567
the person you're
trying to get to is

00:13:08.567 --> 00:13:10.433
moving into different places.

00:13:10.433 --> 00:13:13.700
And this big one.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:14.867
Stop complaining.

00:13:14.867 --> 00:13:16.734
Salespeople aren't
allowed to complain.

00:13:16.734 --> 00:13:18.367
The market is the market.

00:13:18.367 --> 00:13:19.934
Your bosses are your bosses.

00:13:19.934 --> 00:13:24.266
A great salesperson shuts their
mouth and she goes to work every

00:13:24.266 --> 00:13:27.500
day and tries to bring value to
the end-user and is patient and

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.667
over time wins
the marathon of sales.

00:13:29.667 --> 00:13:31.300
Put yourself in that position.

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:35.166
("Unbreakable" by Ben Katz)

